# The build context is source only. Everything below is either large, machine-specific,
# or a credential — and a Docker build context is copied to the daemon whole, so anything
# left in here travels to whatever daemon builds the image.

# Credentials and live state. .docpreview holds the vault, the database and every
# preview's workspace; it is the single most important thing to keep out of an image.
.docpreview/
*.age
*.key

# Build output and caches.
#
# `**/` on each one, not a bare `node_modules/`. A leading pattern with no `**` matches at
# the root only, so `node_modules/` left www/node_modules in the context — 436 MB of it,
# measured, and the whole context was 851 MB against the 3 MB of Go source the build reads.
build.claude/
**/node_modules/
**/.yarn/
**/.docusaurus/
**/build/
**/dist/

# The demo: four Docusaurus checkouts, a 298 MB template they are cloned from, its own
# database and a copy of the binary. None of it is the daemon.
demo/

# Git metadata. The image does not need history, and .git on this repository is large.
.git/
.gitignore

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
